<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>Implementation and Maintenance - activity-app</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.45; margin: 24px; }
    h1 { font-size: 20pt; }
    h2 { font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 18px; }
    h3 { font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 12px; }
    p { font-size: 11pt; }
    ul { margin: 8px 0 8px 20px; }
    pre { background: #f6f8fa; padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #e1e4e8; overflow:auto }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Implementation Details and Maintenance Plan</h1>
  <p>Repository: bannaarisamy-shanmugham-kanini/ac ("activity-app")</p>

  <h2>1. Implementation Details</h2>

  <h3>1.1 Overview</h3>
  <p>
    The project is a client-side single-page application (SPA) built with React and TypeScript using Vite as the build tool. It provides an Activities view and a Projects CRUD flow. State management uses Zustand and persistent storage uses IndexedDB (via the idb library).
  </p>

  <h3>1.2 Tech Stack</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Language: TypeScript</li>
    <li>UI: React</li>
    <li>Build: Vite</li>
    <li>Routing: react-router-dom</li>
    <li>State: Zustand</li>
    <li>Client storage: IndexedDB via idb</li>
    <li>Icons: lucide-react</li>
    <li>CSS: global CSS + utility-class patterns (Tailwind-like class names observed)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>1.3 Project Structure (key files / folders)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>index.html — app entry</li>
    <li>src/main.tsx — React entry point, mounts AppRouter</li>
    <li>src/app/router — Router configuration and AppRouter</li>
    <li>src/app/layout — BaseLayout, Header and layout components</li>
    <li>src/features — feature areas like activity and projects components (list, create, edit, view)</li>
    <li>src/components/ui — shared UI primitives (sheet, buttons, dialogs, sidebar, form inputs)</li>
    <li>src/store — Zustand stores (useAppStore, useProjectStore) and helpers to persist and rehydrate state</li>
    <li>src/lib/db — IndexedDB helpers (db open and schema definition)</li>
    <li>vite.config.ts — Vite config and path alias (@ -> src)</li>
    <li>README.md — project notes and guidance</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>1.4 Data Model & Persistence</h3>
  <p>
    IndexedDB is used with object stores defined as:
  </p>
  <pre>
    DB_NAME = "app-db"
    DB_VERSION = 1
    object stores: "projects", "activities" (keyPath: "id")
  </pre>
  <p>
    Zustand stores hold in-memory state and provide functions to update and set activities and projects. The app includes rehydrateStore and initZustandPersistence paths to rehydrate state from IndexedDB on startup and to persist updates.
  </p>

  <h3>1.5 Routing & UI Flow</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Root path "/" – Activity view</li>
    <li>"/projects" – Projects list</li>
    <li>"/projects/create" – Create project page</li>
    <li>"/projects/edit/:id" – Edit project page</li>
    <li>"/projects/view/:id" – View project page</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>1.6 Build & Run</h3>
  <p>Recommended package.json scripts (example):</p>
  <pre>
    "dev": "vite",
    "build": "vite build",
    "preview": "vite preview",
    "lint": "eslint . --ext .ts,.tsx",
    "test": "vitest"
  </pre>
  <p>Typical steps:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Install dependencies: <code>npm ci</code></li>
    <li>Start dev server: <code>npm run dev</code></li>
    <li>Build production bundle: <code>npm run build</code></li>
    <li>Preview production build: <code>npm run preview</code></li>
  </ol>

  <h3>1.7 Recommended Code Practices</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Pin Node.js version in .nvmrc and in package.json engines.</li>
    <li>Use ESLint + TypeScript rules and Prettier for formatting consistency.</li>
    <li>Use husky + lint-staged to run linters on pre-commit.</li>
    <li>Create unit tests for stores and utilities; component tests for critical UI paths.</li>
    <li>Document public interfaces for stores and DB helpers with TSDoc comments.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Maintenance Details</h2>

  <h3>2.1 Ownership & Contacts</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Primary owner: repository maintainer(s) — include GitHub usernames and email addresses in the project README or MAINTAINERS file.</li>
    <li>Escalation path: Developer -> Team Lead -> On-call Backend/Infra if hosting or CI failures.</li>
    <li>Provide a CODEOWNERS file for automatic review requests on PRs touching core areas.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2.2 Release & Versioning</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Follow semantic versioning for releases if publishing a packaged app or library (MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH).</li>
    <li>Use a CHANGELOG.md and generate entries for each release using tools like "standard-version" or manually maintain changelog entries in PR templates.</li>
    <li>Tag releases in Git and use GitHub Releases to attach build artifacts or release notes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2.3 CI/CD & Deployment</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Configure GitHub Actions to run checks: install -> lint -> typecheck -> tests -> build.</li>
    <li>Deploy static build to a hosting provider: Vercel or Netlify are recommended for SPA previews and production hosting.
      <ul>
        <li>Enable preview deployments for PRs.</li>
        <li>Set build env vars in the hosting platform: NODE_ENV=production, REACT_APP_SENTRY_DSN (if used), etc.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Protect main branch with required status checks and PR review rules.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2.4 Monitoring & Telemetry</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Integrate client-side error reporting (e.g., Sentry) in production builds only. Mask or omit personally identifiable information.</li>
    <li>Set up basic performance checks (Lighthouse) in CI to detect regressions.</li>
    <li>Collect optional usage analytics with user's consent (PostHog or Plausible).</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2.5 Backups & Data Management</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Implement export/import JSON functionality for IndexedDB data (projects and activities) to allow users to back up and restore their data.
      <ul>
        <li>Export should include a schema version and timestamp.</li>
        <li>Import should validate schema version and warn about possible incompatibilities.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>When introducing server-side persistence, implement server-side backups for user data and retention policies.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2.6 Migrations</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Maintain DB_VERSION in src/lib/db/database.ts. When bumping the version, encode migration logic in the openDB upgrade callback to transform object stores or entries safely.</li>
    <li>Test migrations locally and in CI with sample datasets before releasing to users.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2.7 Security Maintenance</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Enable Dependabot or similar for automated dependency updates and security PRs.</li>
    <li>Run npm audit in CI and triage reported vulnerabilities promptly.</li>
    <li>Perform periodic dependency upgrades (quarterly or as needed for critical fixes) and test for regressions.</li>
    <li>Follow secure coding practices: avoid dangerouslySetInnerHTML, validate user-provided data, and use strict CSP headers in the hosting environment.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2.8 Incident Response & Runbooks</h3>
  <h4>Build Failure</h4>
  <ol>
    <li>Check CI logs to identify failing step.</li>
    <li>Run the failing command locally; fix lint/type errors or adjust config.</li>
    <li>Open a PR with the fix and request reviews from CODEOWNERS.</li>
  </ol>

  <h4>Production Errors (Client-side)</h4>
  <ol>
    <li>Review captured Sentry errors or user reports.</li>
    <li>Try to reproduce in a local environment or PR preview deploy.</li>
    <li>Patch, verify in preview, then release to main and monitor for recurrence.</li>
  </ol>

  <h4>Data Corruption</h4>
  <ol>
    <li>Ask user to export current IndexedDB contents (if export available).</li>
    <li>If corruption prevents export, instruct user to temporarily save browser profile and provide screenshots / console logs.</li>
    <li>Provide instructions to clear local storage and re-import from a known-good backup when available.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>2.9 Maintenance Tasks & Schedule</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Weekly: Review dependency alerts and triage security updates.</li>
    <li>Bi-weekly: Review and merge PRs for feature work and bugfixes.
    </li>
    <li>Monthly: Run accessibility and performance audits; update Lighthouse thresholds if necessary.</li>
    <li>Quarterly: Major dependency upgrades and maintenance sprint with full regression testing.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2.10 Documentation & Onboarding</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>README.md: keep updated with local dev, build, test, and backup instructions.</li>
    <li>MAINTAINERS or CODEOWNERS file for clear ownership.</li>
    <li>Developer onboarding doc with: repo structure, how to run locally, common troubleshooting steps, and where to find logs/CI information.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2.11 Useful Scripts & Tools</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>npm run dev — start dev server</li>
    <li>npm run build — create production bundle</li>
    <li>npm run preview — preview production build locally</li>
    <li>npm run lint — run ESLint</li>
    <li>npm run test — run unit tests (Vitest/Jest)</li>
    <li>npx playwright test — run E2E tests (if configured)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Appendices</h2>

  <h3>3.1 Troubleshooting Quick Reference</h3>
  <h4>App does not start in dev</h4>
  <ol>
    <li>Ensure Node version matches .nvmrc or engines.</li>
    <li>Run <code>npm ci</code> to install exact dependencies.</li>
    <li>Check environment variables; run <code>npm run dev</code> and inspect console for errors.</li>
  </ol>

  <h4>State not persisting across reloads</h4>
  <ol>
    <li>Confirm IndexedDB object stores exist via browser DevTools Application > IndexedDB.</li>
    <li>Check console for errors during rehydrateStore and initZustandPersistence calls.</li>
    <li>Validate DB_VERSION and migration code in src/lib/db/database.ts.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>3.2 Example: Export JSON schema (recommended)</h3>
  <pre>
{
  "meta": {
    "app": "activity-app",
    "version": 1,
    "exportedAt": "2026-01-27T00:00:00Z"
  },
  "projects": [ /* array of projects */ ],
  "activities": [ /* array of activities */ ]
}
  </pre>

  <h3>3.3 Contact & Further Work</h3>
  <p>
    If you'd like, I can also:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Open the suggested GitHub issues for CI, export/import, and tests.</li>
    <li>Generate GitHub Actions workflow YAML for CI.
    </li>
    <li>Provide a sample export/import implementation and a small test suite for the stores.
  </ul>

  <p>Document created on 2026-01-27.</p>
